{"nodes": [{"id": "_github_issue_template_bug_report_bug_report_template", "label": "Bug report issue template", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Titled [Bug], labelled bug + priority: medium. Asks up front whether the issue reproduces against an in-memory transport or journal, which rules out a peer-dep mismatch before a maintainer looks."}, {"id": "_github_issue_template_bug_report_optional_peer_checklist", "label": "Optional peer dependency checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Thirteen checkboxes naming the optional peers (better-sqlite3, cassandra-driver, ioredis, memjs, @aws-sdk/client-s3, kafkajs, nats, mqtt, amqplib, @grpc/grpc-js, ws, the HTTP backends, @kubernetes/client-node) \u2014 reporters check only what their code exercises, because the bug may be in the adapter for that integration."}, {"id": "_github_issue_template_bug_report_security_flag", "label": "Security-relevance flag on the bug template", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Points reporters at the [Security] template, which asks for the exploit walkthrough, affected files and disclosure status; either way a maintainer adds the security and severity: labels, because GitHub Forms cannot add them conditionally."}], "edges": [{"source": "_github_issue_template_bug_report_bug_report_template", "target": "_github_issue_template_bug_report_optional_peer_checklist", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": ".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml", "source_locat